        "original_id": "2d937be1-4750-5fb8-abfa-cedd31550c6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Lion and the Horse, Bonanza\n- People: Louis King, Crane Wilbur, Steve Cochran, Ray Teal\n- Animals: Wildfire\n- Roles: Sheriff Roy Coffee\n- Organizations: NBC\n\nFacts:\n- The Lion and the Horse is a 1952 Western film.\n- The Lion and the Horse was directed by Louis King and written by Crane Wilbur.\n- The Lion and the Horse stars Steve Cochran, Ray Teal, and a horse named Wildfire.\n- From 1960 to 1972, Ray Teal's longest-running role was Sheriff Roy Coffee on NBC's western series Bonanza.",
